Create a complete TypeScript module exporting `RemainingFormat` and `formatRemaining`:

```typescript
export interface RemainingFormat {
  separator?: string;
  showDays?: boolean;
}
export function formatRemaining(seconds: number, format?: RemainingFormat): string;
```

`seconds` must be a finite, nonnegative integer; otherwise throw `RangeError`. The default separator is `:` and must be used verbatim, including when it is empty. With `showDays` omitted or false, return `HH<separator>MM<separator>SS`; hours may exceed 23 and must contain at least two digits. With `showDays: true`, return `DD<separator>HH<separator>MM<separator>SS`, where days contains at least two digits and hours is in `00..23`. Minutes and seconds are always two digits. Zero therefore formats as `00:00:00` by default. Do not mutate the optional configuration object.

